        <dc:subject>web applications</dc:subject>
        <dc:subject>penetration testing</dc:subject>
        <dc:subject>owasp</dc:subject>
        <dc:subject>exploit</dc:subject>
        <dc:title>Web Application Penetration Testing with Artificial Intelligence: A Systematic Review</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>ÐPenetration testing is an intricate activity, yet vital for the security of web applications and the protection of user data. Due to its time-consuming nature, recent developments have emphasized the use of artificial intelligence to enhance efficiency, shorten testing times, and substantially improve penetration testing results. By combining artificial intelligence with conventional penetration testing techniques, researchers aim to improve the processes, providing organizations with the means to create stronger web applications. This paper presents a thorough review of research conducted between 2013 and 2024 on the application of artificial intelligence in web application penetration testing. We highlight advancements and challenges in employing learningbased methods to enhance penetration testing, providing a comprehensive overview of the current state and future directions in the field. Our results show that leveraging artificial intelligence has proven to be more efficient than traditional approaches, but they still face significant challenges.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>2024-10-24</dc:date>
        <dc:identifier>
            <dcterms:URI>
                <rdf:value>https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/10945297/</rdf:value>
            </dcterms:URI>
        </dc:identifier>
        <dcterms:dateSubmitted>2026-09-09 15:52:45</dcterms:dateSubmitted>
        <z:shortTitle>Web Application Penetration Testing with Artificial Intelligence</z:shortTitle>
        <z:language>en</z:language>
        <z:libraryCatalog>DOI.org (Crossref)</z:libraryCatalog>
        <dc:rights>https://doi.org/10.15223/policy-029</dc:rights>
        <bib:pages>236-245</bib:pages>
        <bib:presentedAt>
            <bib:Conference>
                <dc:title>2024 22nd International Symposium on Network Computing and Applications (NCA)</dc:title>
            </bib:Conference>
        </bib:presentedAt>
    </rdf:Description>
    <bib:Memo rdf:about="#item_109">
        <rdf:value>&lt;div data-schema-version=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(249, 250, 251);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(21, 21, 23);&quot;&gt;Обзор 49 научных работ (с 2013 по 2024 гг) по применению искусственного интеллекта в пентесте веб-приложений. Рассматриваются методы ML, NLP, RL.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(249, 250, 251);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(21, 21, 23);&quot;&gt;Большинство исследований сосредоточены на этапах сканирования и эксплуатации, чаще всего для обнаружения SQLi и XSS. Выявлены проблемы: нехватка размеченных датасетов, ограниченное применение RL и гибридных методов, слабая воспроизводимость.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(249, 250, 251);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(21, 21, 23);&quot;&gt;Перспективные направления: большие языковые модели (LLM), adversarial-атаки, защита данных.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</rdf:value>
    </bib:Memo>
