        <dc:subject>web applications</dc:subject>
        <dc:subject>use case model</dc:subject>
        <dc:subject>security policy</dc:subject>
        <dc:subject>secure web application</dc:subject>
        <dc:subject>architecture</dc:subject>
        <dc:subject>development methods</dc:subject>
        <dc:title>Agile development of secure web applications</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>A secure system is one that is protected against specific undesired outcomes.Delivering a secure system, and particularly a secure web application, is not easy.Integrating general-purpose information systems development methods withsecurity development activities could be a useful means to surmount thesedifficulties Agile processes, such as Extreme Programming, are of increasing interest insoftware development. Most significantly for web applications, agile processesencourage and embrace requirements change, which is a desirable characteristicfor web application development.In this paper, we present an agile process to deliver secure web applications.The contribution of the research is not the development of a new method or processthat addresses security concerns. Rather, we investigate general-purpose informationsystemdevelopment methods (e.g., Feature-Driven Development (FDD)) and mature security methods, namely risk analysis, and integrate them to address the development of secure web applications. The key features of our approach are(1) a process capable of dealing with the key challenges of web applicationsdevelopment, namely decreasing life-cycle times and frequently changing requirements; and (2) an iterative approach to risk analysis that integrates security design throughout the development process.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>July 11, 2006</dc:date>
        <dc:identifier>
            <dcterms:URI>
                <rdf:value>https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/1145581.1145641</rdf:value>
            </dcterms:URI>
        </dc:identifier>
        <dcterms:dateSubmitted>2026-09-09</dcterms:dateSubmitted>
        <z:libraryCatalog>ACM Digital Library</z:libraryCatalog>
        <bib:pages>305–312</bib:pages>
    </rdf:Description>
    <bib:Memo rdf:about="#item_100">
        <rdf:value>&lt;div data-schema-version=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(249, 250, 251);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(21, 21, 23);&quot;&gt;Авторы предлагают agile-процесс для разработки безопасных веб-приложений, основанный на расширении подхода Feature-Driven Development (FDD) за счёт интеграции итеративного анализа рисков. Ключевая идея - встроить безопасность во все фазы разработки, начиная с определения политики безопасности и заканчивая реализацией. На каждом шаге итерации проводится анализ рисков для всей системы (включая уже существующие функции), что позволяет выявлять новые уязвимости и своевременно их исправлять.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</rdf:value>
    </bib:Memo>
