        <dc:subject>vulnerabilities</dc:subject>
        <dc:subject>web applications</dc:subject>
        <dc:subject>vulnerability detection</dc:subject>
        <dc:title>Efficiency and Effectiveness of Web Application Vulnerability Detection Approaches: A Review</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>Most existing surveys and reviews on web application vulnerability detection (WAVD) approaches focus on comparing and summarizing the approaches’ technical details. Although some studies have analyzed the efficiency and effectiveness of specific methods, there is a lack of a comprehensive and systematic analysis of the efficiency and effectiveness of various WAVD approaches. We conducted a systematic literature review (SLR) of WAVD approaches and analyzed their efficiency and effectiveness. We identified 105 primary studies out of 775 WAVD articles published between January 2008 and June 2019. Our study identified 10 categories of artifacts analyzed by the WAVD approaches and 8 categories of WAVD meta-approaches for analyzing the artifacts. Our study’s results also summarized and compared the effectiveness and efficiency of different WAVD approaches on detecting specific categories of web application vulnerabilities and which web applications and test suites are used to evaluate the WAVD approaches. To our knowledge, this is the first SLR that focuses on summarizing the effectiveness and efficiencies of WAVD approaches. Our study results can help security engineers choose and compare WAVD tools and help researchers identify research gaps.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>October 8, 2021</dc:date>
        <dc:identifier>
            <dcterms:URI>
               <rdf:value>https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3474553</rdf:value>
            </dcterms:URI>
        </dc:identifier>
        <dcterms:dateSubmitted>2026-09-09 16:10:11</dcterms:dateSubmitted>
        <z:shortTitle>Efficiency and Effectiveness of Web Application Vulnerability Detection Approaches</z:shortTitle>
        <z:libraryCatalog>ACM Digital Library</z:libraryCatalog>
        <bib:pages>190:1–190:35</bib:pages>
    </bib:Article>
    <bib:Journal rdf:about="urn:issn:0360-0300">
        <dc:identifier>DOI 10.1145/3474553</dc:identifier>
        <prism:volume>54</prism:volume>
        <dc:title>ACM Comput. Surv.</dc:title>
        <dc:identifier>ISSN 0360-0300</dc:identifier>
        <prism:number>9</prism:number>
    </bib:Journal>
    <bib:Memo rdf:about="#item_103">
        <rdf:value>&lt;div data-schema-version=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(249, 250, 251);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(21, 21, 23);&quot;&gt;Это обзор литературы, в которой говориться об эффективности и производительности подходов к обнаружению уязвимостей веб-приложений (в основном для инъекций SQLi и XSS).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(249, 250, 251);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(21, 21, 23);&quot;&gt;Выводы: большинство работ не предоставляют адекватных оценок, отсутствуют качественные тестовые наборы с известным числом уязвимостей. Это говорит о малой базе исследований в этой области.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</rdf:value>
    </bib:Memo>
