        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_37"/>
        <dc:subject>sql injection</dc:subject>
        <dc:subject>owasp</dc:subject>
        <dc:subject>xss</dc:subject>
        <dc:title>Securing web applications against XSS and SQLi attacks using a novel deep learning approach</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>Several methods can be used to identify SQL injection attacks, including regular expression matching and MLbased models like Support Vector Machine, Naive Bayes, Random Forest, and Decision Tree. Regular expression matching is widely used among these methods due to its high accuracy rate and fast recognition speed. SQL injection attacks have been a consistent focus of network security research and are ranked as the top risk to network applications by the Open Web Application Security Project (OWASP)15. Various methods have been proposed to detect SQL injection in recent years by examining the threats, attack types and modes of attack.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>2024-01-20</dc:date>
        <dc:identifier>
            <dcterms:URI>
                <rdf:value>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-023-48845-4</rdf:value>
            </dcterms:URI>
        </dc:identifier>
        <dcterms:dateSubmitted>2026-09-09 16:12:19</dcterms:dateSubmitted>
        <z:language>en</z:language>
        <z:libraryCatalog>DOI.org (Crossref)</z:libraryCatalog>
        <bib:pages>1803</bib:pages>
    </bib:Article>
    <bib:Journal rdf:about="urn:issn:2045-2322">
        <dc:identifier>DOI 10.1038/s41598-023-48845-4</dc:identifier>
        <prism:volume>14</prism:volume>
        <dc:title>Scientific Reports</dc:title>
        <dc:identifier>ISSN 2045-2322</dc:identifier>
        <prism:number>1</prism:number>
        <dcterms:alternative>Sci Rep</dcterms:alternative>
    </bib:Journal>
    <bib:Memo rdf:about="#item_106">
        <rdf:value>&lt;div data-schema-version=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(249, 250, 251);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(21, 21, 23);&quot;&gt;Предложен новый подход к обнаружению SQL-инъекций и XSS-атак с использованием гибридной нейронной сети CNN+LSTM.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(249, 250, 251);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(21, 21, 23);&quot;&gt;Модель обучается на трёх наборах данных: собственный тестовый стенд (DVWA/bWAPP + Burp Suite), публичный набор SQL/XSS-полезных нагрузок и бенчмарк HTTP CSIC 2010. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(249, 250, 251);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(21, 21, 23);&quot;&gt;Достигнута высокая точность (99.23–99.84%) и низкий уровень ложных срабатываний.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(249, 250, 251);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(21, 21, 23);&quot;&gt;Данный подход может применяться для создания “умного“ WAF (Web Application Firewall) и IDS (Intrusion Detection System) - для выявления подозрительной активности и генерации предупреждений.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</rdf:value>
    </bib:Memo>
